# Vulnerability details

## Impact
If and when the executeAction function reverts at either of the checks, the amount of ETH sent along with the call will be locked in the contract forever, with no current measures of recovery.

## Proof of Concept
executeAction is called, but the call fails at either of the below stages:

```
    if (currentState != ActionState.Queued) revert InvalidActionState(currentState);
    if (block.timestamp < action.minExecutionTime) revert MinExecutionTimeNotReached();
    if (msg.value != actionInfo.value) revert IncorrectMsgValue();
```

Then the ETH sent with the call remains stuck and is not refunded to the caller.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Update the validatePostActionExecution in the ILlamaActionGuard interface.

```
function validatePostActionExecution(ActionInfo calldata actionInfo) external {
    // Perform post-execution validations or checks here

    // Check the balance of the executor
    uint256 executorBalance = address(executor).balance;

    // Refund ETH to the caller if there is a positive balance
    if (executorBalance > 0) {
        payable(msg.sender).transfer(executorBalance);
    }
}
```


