# Vulnerability details

## Impact
#### Delegatecall to targets which have storage access will read/write each other's storage variables.
Although slot 0 is protected from modification by delegatecall, reading slot 0 is not protected.
Modifying storage slot other than 0 is not protected.
It's much better to impose restriction that delegetecallable target will not have access to storage slot except immutable storage.
To make sure that storage slot overlapping does not happen, whitelisting of delegatecallable targets is required.
Just like LlamaCore, `authorizeScript()` function should be added.

