# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Attacker can create action `authorizeScript` to add authorizedScripts for the `target` and then create action and execute action to call the fake target contract and call the `delegatecall()`

## Proof of Concept

As we can see, `LlamaExecutor.execute()` using `delegatecall` without any check eg.(check slot0).
```solidity
  function execute(address target, uint256 value, bool isScript, bytes calldata data)
    external
    returns (bool success, bytes memory result)
  {
    if (msg.sender != LLAMA_CORE) revert OnlyLlamaCore();
    (success, result) = isScript ? target.delegatecall(data) : target.call{value: value}(data);//@audit
  }
}
```

In LlamaCore,there has `authorizeScript()` to add `authorizedScripts` auth. So attacker can create action `authorizeScript` to add authorizedScripts for the `target` and then create action and execute action to call the fake target contract and call the `delegatecall()`
```solidity
  function authorizeScript(address script, bool authorized) external onlyLlama {
    if (script == address(this) || script == address(policy)) revert RestrictedAddress();
    authorizedScripts[script] = authorized;
    emit ScriptAuthorized(script, authorized);
  }
```

